cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "biodeg-rate-methods: three independent estimators of a bulk groundwater attenuation rate"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it."
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Three independent estimators of a bulk attenuation rate for a dissolved groundwater
  contaminant (Mann-Kendall with a Theil-Sen slope, Domenico-normalized concentration
  against distance, and a spatio-temporal penalized spline), kept separate by construction,
  with a literature-prior combine and a MODFLOW 6 handoff writer.
authors:
  # TODO confirm the author list and add ORCIDs before sharing.
  - family-names: Siciliano
    given-names: Steven
    affiliation: "Environmental Material Science Inc."
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: McHugh
        given-names: "Thomas E."
    title: >-
      Forecasting Groundwater Remediation Timeframes: Site-Specific Temporal Monitoring
      Results May Not Predict Future Performance
    journal: "Groundwater Monitoring & Remediation"
    volume: 43
    issue: 4
    start: 92
    end: 103
    year: 2023
    notes: >-
      Title and journal verified against the published record; the volume, issue and page
      range come from the citation recorded in biodeg_rates/prior.py and have not been
      independently checked. The co-author list is not yet filled in. The benzene rate
      figures used in prior.py (median 0.14/yr, n=1905 GeoTracker sites, 5th-95th
      percentile -0.15 to 0.53/yr) are computed from this paper's Data S1.
